 This runbook tests the GUI renderer on one physical GPU before opening the normal Vintage Story client. It uses a disposable copy of the game and a private Pharos scenario, which starts an embedded server and an isolated engine client. It does not open the user's installed game, normal user data directory, or world. The data path must be explicitly set to a child directory inside the disposable staging directory; both scenarios reject missing paths, paths outside `VINTAGE_STORY`, and any symlink/junction in existing components of the stage or data path before starting a server or client.
 
